Add the 68030 to Minimig's CPU menu in Main_MiSTer.

The Minimig core carries a 68030 mode, selected by CPU type code 10 in the
config byte the firmware sends, with the clock in bits 7-6. The firmware could
not reach it: the menu showed that slot as "-----", loading a config corrected
code 10 to 11, and minimig_ConfigCPU masked the byte to six bits so the clock
bits never left the board.

  * config_cpu_msg[2] is "68030", and config_cpu030_msg names the four clocks.
  * The CPU line cycles through eight settings instead of four: 68000, 68010,
    68020 Fast, 68020 ~14MHz, then the 68030 at 25, 40 and 50MHz and
    unthrottled. Nothing else in the menu moves, so no other item is renumbered.
  * The config byte goes out whole.
  * The load-time correction of code 10 is gone. It was there because the code
    was unused; a config selecting the 68030 is now a config selecting the
    68030, and loading one under a core that does not offer it will give an
    undefined CPU - the same as asking any core for something it lacks.
  * The chipset help text mentions the 68030 and says it has no MMU and no FPU.

Applies to Main_MiSTer 5b3ae644069761ef54b92aaa35178771d0d69fec.

    git clone https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Main_MiSTer
    cd Main_MiSTer
    git apply /path/to/main_mister_68030.patch
    make

Both changed files compile clean.

